**`{{ .ProjectName }}` [26.10.1](https://github.com/mariadb-operator/mariadb-operator/releases/tag/26.10.1) is here!** 🦭

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This is a patch release on top of `26.10.0`. Refer to the [26.10.0 release notes](https://github.com/mariadb-operator/mariadb-operator/releases/tag/26.10.0) for the full changelog of the `26.10.x` series.

If you're upgrading from previous versions, __do not miss the [UPGRADE GUIDE](https://github.com/mariadb-operator/mariadb-operator/blob/main/docs/releases/UPGRADE_26.10.1.md)__ for a smooth transition.

## MariaDB major version upgrades

A new optional field `updateStrategy.mariadbAutoUpgradeEnabled` (disabled by default) sets `MARIADB_AUTO_UPGRADE=true` in the `mariadb` container, so the official image entrypoint runs `mariadb-upgrade` on start ([#1921](https://github.com/mariadb-operator/mariadb-operator/pull/1921)). Bumping `spec.image` across a major version (e.g. `mariadb:11.8` to `mariadb:12.3`) requires running this migration: without it, the Pods restart in place against an unmigrated datadir and every query touching `mysql.proc` fails. Set the flag **before** bumping the image:

```yaml
apiVersion: k8s.mariadb.com/v1alpha1
kind: MariaDB
metadata:
  name: mariadb
spec:
  image: mariadb:12.3.3
  updateStrategy:
    mariadbAutoUpgradeEnabled: true
```

Leaving it set afterwards is safe: `mariadb-upgrade` is a no-op when there is nothing to migrate.

## MaxScale filters

[MaxScale](https://github.com/mariadb-operator/mariadb-operator/blob/main/docs/maxscale.md#filter-configuration) now supports [filters](https://mariadb.com/docs/maxscale/reference/maxscale-filters), which let you reject, alter or log requests before they reach the router and before the response is sent back to the client ([#1923](https://github.com/mariadb-operator/mariadb-operator/pull/1923)). Declare them in `spec.filters` and reference them by name from `spec.services[].filters`, in the order they should be applied:

```yaml
apiVersion: k8s.mariadb.com/v1alpha1
kind: MaxScale
metadata:
  name: maxscale
spec:
  filters:
    - name: throttle
      module: throttlefilter
      params:
        max_qps: "500"
        throttling_duration: 60000ms
  services:
    - name: rw-router
      router: readwritesplit
      filters:
        - throttle
      listener:
        port: 3306
```

Filters are never applied implicitly: a filter declared in `spec.filters` but not referenced by any service is loaded and left unused. The same release also adds `spec.volumes` to the `MaxScale` Pod template, which pairs with the existing `spec.volumeMounts` so you can mount extra `ConfigMaps`, `Secrets` or ephemeral storage into the MaxScale container.

Kudos to @hedgieinsocks for driving this feature end to end!

